<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <title>CEM App — Choose a flow</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:wght@400;700;900&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <main class="landing">
        <header class="landing-hero">
            <span class="eyebrow">Okta CEM Reference App</span>
            <h1>Two paths to entitlement governance.</h1>
            <p>This app implements the same end goal — Okta governing access to a custom application — through two distinct integration models. Pick a flow to demo.</p>
        </header>

        <section class="flow-grid">
            <% const byo = flows.find(f => f.key === 'byo') || { configured: false }; %>
            <a class="flow-card theme-byo <%= byo.configured ? '' : 'disabled' %>"
               href="<%= byo.configured ? '/byo' : '#' %>"
               aria-disabled="<%= !byo.configured %>">
                <span class="flow-tag">Path A · BYO</span>
                <h2>BYO Entitlements</h2>
                <p class="flow-summary">Plain SAML 2.0 + IGA-managed entitlement attributes. Catalog values live in Okta, grants flow at SAML login. No SCIM provisioning.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Okta IGA Entitlement Management defines attribute values</li>
                    <li>SAML attribute statements <code>appuser.access</code> + <code>appuser.role</code></li>
                    <li>App reads grants from <code>req.user.attributes</code></li>
                </ul>
                <span class="flow-cta">
                    <%= byo.configured ? 'Try the BYO demo →' : 'Not configured — add via /admin/integrations' %>
                </span>
            </a>

            <% const scim = flows.find(f => f.key === 'scim') || { configured: false }; %>
            <a class="flow-card theme-scim <%= scim.configured ? '' : 'disabled' %>"
               href="<%= scim.configured ? '/scim' : '#' %>"
               aria-disabled="<%= !scim.configured %>">
                <span class="flow-tag">Path B · SCIM</span>
                <h2>Governance with SCIM 2.0</h2>
                <p class="flow-summary">Okta IGA discovers the catalog from the app, and SCIM-PATCHes user grants in real time. Bidirectional, full IGA features.</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Okta imports <code>/scim/v2/Roles</code> + <code>/scim/v2/Entitlements</code></li>
                    <li>App receives grants via SCIM PATCH on <code>/Users/{id}</code></li>
                    <li>Dashboard reads grants from the local DB</li>
                </ul>
                <span class="flow-cta">
                    <%= scim.configured ? 'Try the SCIM demo →' : 'Not configured — add via /admin/integrations' %>
                </span>
            </a>
        </section>

        <p class="landing-footer">
            Hosted at <code><%= host %></code>. Manage integrations at <code>/admin/integrations</code>.
        </p>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
